{"seq":1,"mint":"C5","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":false,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"the block's timestamp is the one that set its current text","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F4"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"pub struct Block {\n    pub id: String,\n    pub heading: bool,\n    pub level: Option<u8>,\n    pub text: String,\n    pub cite: Vec<String>,\n    pub revisions: usize,\n}","why":"The current Block type has no timestamp field, so it cannot retain a timestamp identifying which event set its current text.","quoted":true},{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"whether that was its `Create` or its last `Revise`","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F4"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"ProseEvent::Create { id, heading, level, text, cite, before, .. } => {\n                // Insert at the anchor if it is still present; otherwise\n                // append. A dangling anchor cannot reorder silently — the\n                // block lands at the end, where its absence is visible.\n                match before.as_deref().and_then(|b| order.iter().position(|o| o == b)) {\n                    Some(at) => order.insert(at, id.clone()),\n                    None => order.push(id.clone()),\n                }\n                by_id.insert(id.clone(), Block { id, heading, level, text, cite, revisions: 0 });\n            }\n            ProseEvent::Revise { id, text, cite, .. } => {\n                if let Some(b) = by_id.get_mut(&id) {\n                    b.text = text;","why":"Both event handlers ignore their timestamp fields, and the resulting Block stores no timestamp; neither Create nor the last Revise supplies a retained block timestamp.","quoted":true}],"at":1790112488,"cost":0.02841921,"elapsed_ms":196507,"attempts":4,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0}
